hypotheses.statement:
Let $(U_1,U_2,U_3)$ and $(W_1,W_2,W_3)$ be independent uniform ordered partitions of finite labeled sets $U$ and $W$, with all six block sizes prescribed. For arbitrary real functions $g_i=g_i(U_i,W_i)$, $$\label{row:fixed-variance}
 \operatorname{Var}\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^3 g_i\Bigr)
 \le 2\sum_{i=1}^3\operatorname{Var}(g_i).$$

Fix row and column sums for binary matrices with three rows, and take the uniform distribution on the nonempty set of all matrices with these prescribed margins. Let $S_i$ denote row $i$. For arbitrary real row functions $f_i$, $$\label{row:main-variance}
 \operatorname{Var}\Bigl(\sum_{i=1}^3f_i(S_i)\Bigr)
 \le 2\sum_{i=1}^3\operatorname{Var}(f_i(S_i)).$$

Let $N\ge0$ and $0\le q\le N$ be integers. Give $$\mathcal X_{N,q}
 =\left\{x\in\{0,1\}^N:\ \sum_{i=1}^N x_i=q\right\}$$ the uniform measure. Let $\tau_{ij}$ interchange coordinates $i,j$, and put $$G=\frac12\sum_{i<j}(I-\tau_{ij}).$$ For each pair $i<j$, let $Q_{ij}$ be orthogonal projection onto the centered function $$z_{ij}=\mathbf 1_{\{x_i=x_j\}}
            -\mathbb P(x_i=x_j),$$ with the convention $Q_{ij}=0$ when $z_{ij}=0$. Then $$S:=\sum_{i<j}Q_{ij}\preceq G.
 \label{sl:operator-comparison}$$

